ggestions are answered.\n- Suggestion 1 (refuse the harness from any worktree): at fd4ac52 the run with IDH_ROOT set to the review worktree accepted a folder in the primary checkout (rc=0, printed <redacted>/.agents). At 877e3d3 the same run is refused (rc=1, \"refused: folder inside the harness\"). All four harness cases are refused at 877e3d3.\n- Suggestion 2 (refuse a folder outside any repository by name): at 877e3d3 a folder outside any repository now prints \"refused: not in any project\". A folder in another project still prints that project's toplevel, unchanged.\n\nFindings (none blocking; both checked by gaze with its own runs):\n1. consider: skills/replicate/SKILL.md:54 (correctness, confirmed by the snippet check). The new refusal only echoes; it does not exit. The \"not in any project\" case exits rc=0 at 877e3d3. At fd4ac52 it exited 128 from git. The harness refusal two lines up uses `exit 1`. If the line becomes `|| { echo \"refused: not in any project\"; exit 1; }`, the two refusals behave the same and a caller that checks the exit status stops. git's `fatal:` line still goes to stderr. The reader does see \"refused\", so this falls below the bar.\n2. consider: skills/replicate/SKILL.md:51 (correctness, reproduced by gaze). The new H fails open where the old one failed closed. With IDH_ROOT=/nonexistent, git errors and H becomes \".\". A harness folder is then accepted (rc=0, prints <redacted>/.agents). The old snippet refused it (rc=1), by accident: an empty H matched every path. A guard such as `[ -n \"$H\" ] && [ \"$H\" != . ] || exit 1` closes it. The scenario needs a broken IDH_ROOT, which the skill's own preamble sets, so this falls below the bar.\n3. nofollow: skills/replicate/SKILL.md:50 (correctness). `dirname` of the common dir is the primary checkout only for a non-bare, non-submodule repository whose worktrees sit under it. That holds for this harness's `.claude/worktrees` layout. The comment on line 50 also names H a line before it is d